    },
    "body": "References #434 #245. The pre-declared control run: **arm ZB (zeta band-matched) 0.2564 — fails the ≥0.5×Z bar (0.4466); arm CF (content vectors full-width) 0.8948 — ABOVE zeta's 0.8932.** The 0.89 headline was vector fullness, not zeta geometry; the state evolution contributes −0.0016. Verdict: RE-ATTRIBUTED TO BANDING, per the rule.\n\n**The actionable finding: the #245 storage path keeps only one active_range band (1/16th) of each stored vector, costing ~0.66 MRR vs full-width on this corpus (0.2348 → 0.8948).** De-banding storage is an engineering change with a measured ~3.8× retrieval upside, cascading directly into router anchor accuracy. All parity checks (46,938) tie the reconstructed band to the stored vectors. Zeta-anchor task correctly skipped (would be full-width retrieval renamed).",
